{
  "design": "API: code/retry_delay.py exports the pure function retry_delay(attempt, base_seconds, max_seconds). attempt must be a Python int, excluding bool, and at least 1. Seconds accept Python int or float values, excluding bool; integers must be positive and floats must be positive and finite. All invalid inputs raise ValueError. Validate every argument before any early return. No fixed return type is promised.\n\nAlgorithm: Set k = attempt - 1. If base_seconds >= max_seconds, return the supplied cap. Otherwise represent both values by exact integer ratios and form the positive numerator N and denominator D of max_seconds/base_seconds. Since N > D, let t be their bit-length difference. The cap threshold is t when N <= D shifted left by t bits, otherwise t + 1. This computes ceil(log2(max_seconds/base_seconds)) without floating-point logarithms. If k reaches the threshold, return the supplied cap immediately. Never construct 2 ** k for a capped attempt; intermediate integer sizes depend on the numeric inputs, not the attempt magnitude.\n\nFor an uncapped result, scale an integer base using a bounded left shift. Scale a float base using math.ldexp, then apply the cap comparison to the rounded result. If the exact uncapped float-derived value exceeds the finite float range because the cap is a larger integer, return the exact scaled value as a standard-library Fraction instead of overflowing. Results are therefore int, float, or an exceptional Fraction.\n\nOwnership: The helper owns validation and delay calculation only. The job runner owns sleeping, retry limits, job execution, persistence, scheduling, and protection against duplicate side effects. The helper has no mutable state, jitter, configuration, network calls, retry framework, or external dependencies.\n\nTests: code/test_retry_delay.py uses standard-library unittest. Cover the first attempt, doubling, exact and overshot caps, base at or above cap, and attempt 10 ** 100. Cover fractional floats, cap-boundary neighbors, extreme finite floats, large integers, and an uncapped value beyond float range. Reject zero/negative attempts, non-integer attempts, booleans in every position, zero/negative seconds, strings, None, complex values, NaN, and both infinities. Verify validation still runs on immediately capped paths. Implementation and tests will be created in the build stage, entirely under code/.",
